<title>UK: Unilever chairman repeats pro-Europe call.</title>
<headline>Unilever chairman repeats pro-Europe call.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain must take an active part in shaping Europe and the move towards European Economic and Monetary Union, or inward investment will suffer, the chairman of the Anglo-Dutch detergent-to-foods giant Unilever said.</p>
<p>&quot;If the UK continues to create the impression that it may opt out of the European mainstream this will adversely affect inward investment,&quot; said Niall Fitzgerald, who is also chairman of the Confederation of British Industry's Europe Committee.</p>
<p>He made the statement in response to a query from Reuters about his reaction to remarks made by Toyota president Hiroshi Okuda on Wednesday.</p>
</text>
